"""GT-USB-7010ASV - USB Type-C receptacle, USB 2.0, 16 pins, horizontal SMD.

Bare connector: the CC pull-downs, D+/D- series parts and VBUS protection
belong to the board.

Datasheet: G-Switch drawing "Horizontal Type-c 16P Female Short edition SMT
CH=1.68 L=7.35mm", molde code GT-USB-7010ASV, rev A0 (2023-02-04), LCSC
C2988369.

Pins (drawing pin table): A1/B12 and B1/A12 GND, A4/B9 and B4/A9 VBUS, A5 CC1,
B5 CC2, A6/B6 D+, A7/B7 D-, A8 SBU1, B8 SBU2. The footprint pads carry the
contact names; the paired contacts share one pad (A4B9, B4A9, A1B12, B1A12).
Pads 1-4 are the four through-hole shell tabs (SHIELD).

Ratings (drawing, "G-Switch USB-C Specification"): 3 A on VBUS, 1.25 A on
VCONN, 0.25 A on the other contacts; 24 V AC voltage rating; contact resistance
40 mOhm max; -40 to +85 C.

Mechanics: the recommended PCB layout has two 0.65 mm non-plated holes for the
housing pegs (5.78 mm apart, on the shell-tab side of the signal row). The
footprint draws them on F.Fab and User.1 only (no drill): the board outline
must cut them.

Symbol pin types: the cable is the source of the VBUS net, so VBUS pad A4B9 is
power_out; VBUS pad B4A9 is passive, because KiCad ERC reports two power
outputs on one net as a conflict even within one symbol. The shell and GND
contacts are passive; signal contacts are bidirectional.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Usb2")

# Drawing, specification 1: 24 V AC voltage rating of the contacts.
VBUS = io(Power(voltage="0V to 24V"))
GND = io(Ground)
SHIELD = io(Net)
CC1 = io(Net)
CC2 = io(Net)
SBU1 = io(Net)
SBU2 = io(Net)
USB = io(Usb2)

Component(
    name="GT-USB-7010ASV",
    prefix="U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="GT-USB-7010ASV.kicad_sym"),
    part=Part(mpn="GT-USB-7010ASV", manufacturer="G-Switch"),
    pins={
        "VBUS": VBUS,
        "GND": GND,
        "SHIELD": SHIELD,
        "CC1": CC1,
        "CC2": CC2,
        "SBU1": SBU1,
        "SBU2": SBU2,
        "D+": USB.D.P,
        "D-": USB.D.N,
    },
)
